{"name":"Tropical Tree","hex":"#20aea7","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tropical","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or pertaining to the tropics, the equatorial region between 23 degrees north and 23 degrees south.","From, or similar to, a hot, humid climate."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tropical plant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tropical"},{"term":"tree","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A perennial woody plant taller and larger than a shrub with a wooden trunk and, at some distance from the ground, having leaves and branches.","Any other plant (such as a large shrub or herb) that is reminiscent of the above in form and size."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To chase (an animal or person) up a tree.","To place in a tree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tree"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tropical vegetation","blocks":[{"text":"Tropical vegetation, plant life that occurs in climates that are warm year-round, is in general more biologically diverse than in other latitudes. Some tropical areas may receive abundant rain the whole year round, while others have long dry seasons which last several months and may vary in length and intensity with geographic location. These seasonal droughts have a great impact on the vegetation, such as in the Madagascar spiny forests."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Starr_011104-0052_Scaevola_taccada.jpg/330px-Starr_011104-0052_Scaevola_taccada.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tropical_vegetation","wikidata":"Q7846186"},{"title":"Tropics","blocks":[{"text":"The tropics are the region of Earth surrounding the equator, where the Sun may shine directly overhead. This contrasts with the temperate or polar regions of Earth, where the Sun can never be directly overhead. Because of Earth's axial tilt, the width of the tropics is twice the tilt. The tropics are also referred to as the tropical zone and the torrid zone."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/World_map_indicating_tropics_and_subtropics.png/330px-World_map_indicating_tropics_and_subtropics.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tropics","wikidata":"Q42530"},{"title":"Tree","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, a tree is a perennial plant with an elongated stem, or trunk, usually supporting branches and leaves. In some usages, the definition of a tree may be narrower, e.g., including only woody plants with secondary growth, only plants that are usable for timber, or only plants above a specified height. Wider definitions include taller palms, tree ferns, bananas, and bamboos."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Usamljeni_jasen_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Usamljeni_jasen_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tree","wikidata":"Q10884"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Parque_Nacional_do_Itatiaia_floresta.jpg/500px-Parque_Nacional_do_Itatiaia_floresta.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Parque_Nacional_do_Itatiaia_floresta.jpg/500px-Parque_Nacional_do_Itatiaia_floresta.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dense rainforest vegetation in the Itatiaia National Park in Brazil.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AParque_Nacional_do_Itatiaia_floresta.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Tropical_vegetation.jpg/500px-Tropical_vegetation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Tropical_vegetation.jpg/500px-Tropical_vegetation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Typical Caribbean vegetation in Cuba.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATropical_vegetation.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Pedro_II_of_Brazil_by_Rugendas_1846_original.jpg/500px-Pedro_II_of_Brazil_by_Rugendas_1846_original.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Pedro_II_of_Brazil_by_Rugendas_1846_original.jpg/1280px-Pedro_II_of_Brazil_by_Rugendas_1846_original.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Pedro_II_of_Brazil_by_Rugendas_1846_original.jpg/500px-Pedro_II_of_Brazil_by_Rugendas_1846_original.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Emperor Pedro II of Brazil surrounded by tropical vegetation at Quinta da Boa Vista, 1846","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APedro_II_of_Brazil_by_Rugendas_1846_original.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Bora_Bora.jpg/500px-Bora_Bora.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Bora_Bora.jpg/500px-Bora_Bora.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Aerial view of Bora Bora in French Polynesia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABora_Bora.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Kota_Kinabalu_by_Dale_Preston.jpg/500px-Kota_Kinabalu_by_Dale_Preston.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Kota_Kinabalu_by_Dale_Preston.jpg/1280px-Kota_Kinabalu_by_Dale_Preston.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_camp